cd /workspaces/mapan-journeyFrom 426d27d82c251ad5ca1e049f6110988c9d9ae590 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 00:35:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Replace check-in with 32-item instrument (5 dimensions) +
 population z-score levels

- data.js: QUESTIONS replaced with the revised 32-item instrument (Keuangan,
  Psikologis, Kesehatan, Sosial, Spiritual/Makna Hidup). Sosial is a new
  standalone domain, separate from the 4 journey Terminals, no longer tied
  to 'Next Chapter'. Added CHECKIN_DOMAINS metadata (label + color per
  domain) since 'sosial' has no matching Terminal/tone().
- CheckIn.jsx: renders all 32 items grouped under a sticky-progress header
  per dimension; scoring math unchanged (still 0-100 average per domain).
- New statsHelper.js: fetches population stats from mapan_checkin_results,
  computes z-score per domain, and buckets it into 5 readiness levels
  (Perlu Perhatian / Mulai Berkembang / Cukup Siap / Siap / Sangat Siap)
  using standard-normal-ish bands. Falls back to nothing until at least
  MIN_POPULATION (30) respondents exist, since mean/SD from a tiny sample
  isn't meaningful.
- Result.jsx (participant's own phone): shows the 5 domains; once >=30
  people have checked in, shows their level relative to everyone else
  instead of an absolute band, with a disclaimer that this is relative
  standing, not a personal diagnosis. Falls back to the old absolute-score
  bands below that threshold.
- Dashboard.jsx (facilitator/projector): now shows, per domain, the
  population average PLUS a stacked bar of what % of all respondents fall
  in each level -- aggregate only, no individual names (per prior request).
- store.js: syncCheckinResult now writes sosial_score instead of the
  removed next_score.
- Supabase migration: added sosial_score column to mapan_checkin_results
  (next_score column kept, just unused, for backward compatibility).
